rooms_desc ({"       **** WELCOME TO THE HOUSE OF SPANGLE ****You find yourself standing in the middle of a rather strange hallway, this     doesn't really surprise you because you realise it is Spangle's house after    all!. The walls are covered in PICTUREs which are all numbered for easy indexinYour eyes are drawn upwards to the ceiling where you are amazed to find loadsof little pieces of rock bolted to the ceiling so that Spangle can practicefalling off of routes without getting cold or wet, or maybe he just can't bebothered cleaning the floor ever!There are doors leading off in every direction but one inparticular catches your attention. TheDOOR to the south is made ofglass and light floods in and fills your soul with happiness and joy...Cringe!","On entering the bedroom you realise there is something missing.....A bed!There is a lot of Scafolding in this room but why?Under the scafolding you can see a DESK and books but it looks a real tip.Photographs of climbing exploits cover the walls, you can look at them if      you are really interested in that sort of thing. There is a certain musty climbng smell about this room and hence why the WINDOW is always opennot just for   cats to jump out of!","You have entered the most sacred room in the house....The Bathroom.Here you can while away the hours in a lovely SWIMMING POOL with a rather novelWATER SLIDE. Alternatively you could maybe just utilise the big white TELEPHONEin the corner to speak to Hughie or Ralph after a heavy day in the Bar.","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.","You open the patio doors and step outside into the warm sunshine.There are MOUNTAINS all around you covered in heather of different shades ofbrown and red. You hear a distant sound of bagpipes ecoing up the glen, brokennow and then by the familiar sound of GROUSE warbling in the heather.There is a loch stretching halfway down the glen infront of you, the surfaceis like a sheet of glass, reflecting and distorting every detail of themountains along either bank. The sun is reflecting off the surface straightonto your face making your skin feel healthy and warm...you feel as if you want to stay here for ever to recover from your wounds.In the corner of your eye, you notice a wee furry animal scurrying about inthe heather, WOW! you have actually seen a live HAGGIS. Because it has two feet shorter than the other two, you start chasing it the wrng way round the hill and it falls over, rolls down the hill and drowns in the och!","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.",0,})
